In an abstract class, debug mode highlights the abstract member `init(): void` from its name, leaving the `abstract` keyword before it plain, and the concrete `run(): void` through its signature.
== args
--debug
input/abstract-class.ts
== file input/abstract-class.ts
abstract class Base {
  abstract init(): void;
  run(): void {
    this.init();
  }
}
== stdout
«abstract class Base» {
  abstract «init(): void»;
  «run(): void» {
    this.init();
  }
}
== stderr
== exit 0
